# Design: FormedCore, one module for what the Core holds while formed

## Which caller dominates

Counts from rg on `.accessor()` calls, split by gametest versus the rest of main:

| Accessor | GameTests | Main callers |
|---|---|---|
| lastScan | 15 | 6 (JadeInfo 3, CoreMenu 2, PlanterMenu 1) |
| meStatus | 11 | 3 |
| outputs | 8 | 6 |
| power | 6 | 8 |
| multiblock | 6 | 4 |
| fertilizer | 3 | 4 |
| items | 0 | 3 |
| allPartsLoaded, tickOffset | 0 | 0 outside the Core |

- **By call sites,** GameTests dominate, led by `lastScan()`. They stay mechanical edits, and `lastScan()` is Core scan state rather than formed state, so it stays on the Core.
- **By runtime volume,** `tickPlanters` dominates. It runs for every Core every tick and touches all six fields. Doorway queries are capability-cached until `invalidateCapabilities`. The screen builds a table about once per open or refresh.
- I optimise for `tickPlanters`. The rarer callers (screen, Jade, GameTests) pay a little more.

## 1. Interface

```java
package ...multiblock;

/** What a Core holds while its Multiblock is Formed, or Formed-but-paused (ADR 0009). */
public final class FormedCore {
  public record Totals(long stored, long capacity, long fertilizer, int outputFill, MeStatus me) {
    public static final Totals NONE = new Totals(0, 0, 0, 0, MeStatus.NONE);
  }

  /** Looks up the part block entities and builds the pools. The caller guarantees every part is loaded. */
  public static FormedCore build(Level level, Multiblock multiblock, Runnable onStale);

  /** Same Multiblock, no pools, no ME link. Nothing in it touches a block entity. */
  public FormedCore paused();

  /** Ticks the planters and runs ME transfers. A no-op while paused or while any part is unloaded. */
  public void tick(ServerLevel level, int tickOffset);

  /** False while paused. This is the only remote-open membership test. */
  public boolean ownsPlanter(BlockPos pos);

  public List<BlockPos> planters();      // kept while paused, so stopPlanters can run
  public Totals totals();                // Totals.NONE while paused
  public @Nullable EnergyHandler energy();                 // null while paused
  public @Nullable ResourceHandler<ItemResource> items();  // null while paused

  // Test and Core internals only, null while paused
  public Multiblock multiblock();
  public @Nullable PowerPool power();
  public @Nullable FertilizerPool fertilizer();
  public @Nullable OutputSink outputs();
}
```

**Invariants and ordering**
- `tick` calls `power.refillFrom(me)` first. It then ticks planters in `multiblock.planters()` order, and runs the ME transfers only on `ME_INTERVAL` ticks.
- `onStale` fires when a pooled block entity or the ME link is found removed. The Core marks itself dirty, forces a rebuild, and replaces its FormedCore.
- Error mode: a removed member is treated as absent for that call. Nothing throws.
- The MeLink contract is untouched.

`CoreBlockEntity` keeps one field, `@Nullable FormedCore formedCore`, plus `lastScan`, `dirty` and `poolsStale`.

```java
public ScanResult<BlockPos> lastScan();
public void markDirty();
public List<BlockPos> planters();
public boolean ownsPlanter(BlockPos pos) { return formedCore != null && formedCore.ownsPlanter(pos); }
public Totals totals() { return formedCore == null ? Totals.NONE : formedCore.totals(); }
public @Nullable EnergyHandler energy() { return formedCore == null ? null : formedCore.energy(); }
public @Nullable ResourceHandler<ItemResource> items() { return formedCore == null ? null : formedCore.items(); }
public @Nullable FormedCore formedCore();   // for GameTests
```

In `scan()`, the WAITING_FOR_CHUNKS branch becomes `formedCore = formedCore == null ? null : formedCore.paused();`. The other branch becomes `formedCore = result.formed() ? FormedCore.build(level, Multiblock.from(result), this::markPoolsStale) : null;`. `level.invalidateCapabilities(worldPosition)` still runs after either.

## 2. Usage

```java
// CoreBlockEntity.tickPlanters: the whole method
if (formedCore != null) formedCore.tick(level, tickOffset());

// CoreMenu.buildTable
Totals t = core.totals();
... new Totals(scan.formed(), ..., t.stored(), t.capacity(), draw, t.fertilizer(), t.outputFill(), t.me());
for (BlockPos pos : core.planters()) { ... }

// CoreMenu.openPlanter and PlanterMenu.stillInCoreStructure
if (!core.ownsPlanter(pos)) return;
```

## 3. What the implementation hides

- Null-checking of the four pools and the ME link.
- Pool construction: block-entity lookup by type, `PowerPool`, `FertilizerPool`, `OutputSink`, and the ME link lookup.
- The `onStale` wiring.
- The `allPartsLoaded` check inside `tick`.
- The online and removed ME logic.
- `TickContext` assembly.
- The combined item handler, which currently sits in `DoorwayHandlers.items(fertilizer, outputs)`. It moves in as a private method.

## 4. Dependency strategy

- **In-process.** The pools and `Multiblock` are plain objects and need no adapter.
- **Local-substitutable.** Block entities are reached through the real `Level`, and GameTests run against a real one. No seam is added.
- **MeLink is the only seam.** It has two adapters, the AE2 one and the fake in the tests, so it is real under ADR 0005. FormedCore receives the link from the pool build and does not widen it.
- **No new seam.** There is one FormedCore, and nobody varies it.

## 5. Trade-offs

**Leverage is high** at `tickPlanters`, which drops from about 25 lines to 1, and at the two membership checks, which collapse into one test. `buildTable` goes from four null checks to one `totals()` call.

**Leverage is thin** in the GameTests. They go through `core.formedCore().outputs()` and similar, one extra hop. The Core's pass-throughs `energy()` and `items()` are one-liners again. They let the capability registration stay a plain `be::energy`.

**CoreBlockEntity accessors**
- Kept: `lastScan`, `markDirty`, `serverTick`, `onLoad`, `preRemoveSideEffects`.
- Added: `planters`, `ownsPlanter`, `totals`, `energy`, `items`, `formedCore`.
- Removed: `multiblock`, `power`, `fertilizer`, `outputs`, `meStatus` (now `totals().me()`), `allPartsLoaded` (hidden in `tick`).
- `tickOffset` becomes private.

**DoorwayHandlers** is deleted. The deletion test says `energy(core)` and `items(core)` were pass-throughs and vanish. The combiner moves into FormedCore. `MPBlockEntities` registers `(be, side) -> be.energy()` and `(be, side) -> be.items()`.

**Behaviour preserved**
- `ownsPlanter` is false while paused, matching the old `lastScan().formed()` check.
- Pause and resume rebuild the pools exactly as today.
- Membership is still checked only on the server.
- Jade still reads only `lastScan()`, with no Jade imports.

**Risk.** Replacing the FormedCore object on rebuild invalidates any reference a caller holds across ticks. The only holder is the capability cache, and `invalidateCapabilities` already covers that.

